Last v6-brief item. Reframes Plans as work folders and wires the bidirectional link.

- Plans → Work folders: each folder is a bundle card (plan · tasks · decisions ·
  docs) with its files as chips that open the in-render markdown reader; renamed the
  nav/title "Plans" → "Work folders" (route id + #/work/:slug reader unchanged).
- Bidirectional link (grounded, not fuzzy): a work-link index built in rebuild()
  from issues that cite `docs/work/<slug>` in their body/design/notes (20 issues →
  6 folders here). Work-folder cards show their linked epic/tasks (chips → detail);
  the issue/epic detail hub's Work-folder slot is now a real link → the reader.
- Honest SEAM (56461780) for folders/issues without a citation — no fuzzy matching.

Dark-default, mono, routing (cards/chips are entity links), one-card grammar.
Interaction-verified: 93 bundle cards, 287 file chips, 6 real linked folders + 87
SEAMs, folder→reader, linked-issue chip→detail, issue detail→work folder→reader.
ESLint clean, 12 tests pass. Screenshot: v6-plans-workfolders.png.

v6-brief now feature-complete pending the data SEAMs (7dc229d4 lease/surface,
f61601ab stage_runs, 56461780 work-graph, c7971150 Graphiti). Refs f4a421d7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
